    "tier": 1,
    "type": "standard",
    "notes": "<h3 data-section-id=\"mb5v8a\" data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1285\">Personality</h3><p data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1620\">Torque is the most approachable member of Dead Current. He's a mechanic first and a runner second. He loves machines, drones, engines, and gadgets with the enthusiasm of a hobbyist who somehow wandered into organized crime. Despite his size and intimidating appearance, he's surprisingly patient and enjoys explaining how things work.</p><h3 data-section-id=\"1r0j58p\" data-start=\"1622\" data-end=\"1638\">Scene Detail</h3><p data-start=\"1639\" data-end=\"1728\">Names all of his drones and becomes visibly irritated if somebody calls them \"equipment.\"</p><h3 data-section-id=\"emdch2\" data-start=\"1730\" data-end=\"1745\">Catchphrase</h3><blockquote data-start=\"1746\" data-end=\"1800\"><p data-start=\"1748\" data-end=\"1800\">\"I can fix that. Might make it worse first, though.\"</p></blockquote><h3 data-section-id=\"ie5x6g\" data-start=\"1802\" data-end=\"1812\">Accent</h3><p data-start=\"1813\" data-end=\"1873\">Working-class American. Slight Seattle dockworker influence.</p>",
